{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>התעו אותי אלהים.</b> [They caused me to wander] — the holy tongue [i.e., this is the usage of the sacred language], and the meaning is that one journeys from place to place and does not know where he is going; likewise \"והנה תועה בשדה\" (Genesis 37:15), and this is not straying of the heart; likewise it is written \"למה תתענו ד׳\" (Isaiah 63:17)." "<b>אמרי לי.</b> [Say of me] — on my account. Likewise \"ואמר פרעה לבני ישראל\" (Exodus 14:3)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:15.364602761Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}